  "description": "<p>The RO-BagIt profile (<a href=\"https://github.com/ResearchObject/bagit-ro\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/ResearchObject/bagit-ro</a>) calls for the tag manifest to be used to specify additional files to be included in the bag as annotations or provenance for the primary objects of the data directory.  (See example <a href=\"https://github.com/ResearchObject/bagit-ro/blob/master/example1/tagmanifest-sha1.txt\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/ResearchObject/bagit-ro/blob/master/example1/tagmanifest-sha1.txt</a>) </p>\n\n<p>The import/export tool right now seems only to support export of the tag manifest, containing hard-coded key/value pairs from the BagConfig (per <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export/blob/master/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/importexport/exporter/Exporter.java#L141-L142\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export/blob/master/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/importexport/exporter/Exporter.java#L141-L142</a>). It seems to completely ignore this file on import.</p>\n\n<p>In order to import a bag that adhered to the profile, I think it would need to be able to parse the supplied tag manifest and import the files identified therein</p>",
